{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Wilkes-Liberty/shared-ci/pulls/24","id":4898120587,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTr2yLc8AAAABI_Njiw","html_url":"https://github.com/Wilkes-Liberty/shared-ci/pull/24","diff_url":"https://github.com/Wilkes-Liberty/shared-ci/pull/24.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Wilkes-Liberty/shared-ci/pull/24.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Wilkes-Liberty/shared-ci/issues/24","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Wilkes-Liberty/shared-ci/pulls/24/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Wilkes-Liberty/shared-ci/pulls/24/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Wilkes-Liberty/shared-ci/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Wilkes-Liberty/shared-ci/issues/24/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Wilkes-Liberty/shared-ci/statuses/b2c6f71dfb3b57cd70690b6032247be0d2fd020a","number":24,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"DEV-1009: Keep CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY markers when stripping PR bodies","user":{"login":"jmcerda","id":4259312,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNTkzMTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4259312?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcerda","html_url":"https://github.com/jmcerda","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcerda/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcerda/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcerda/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcerda/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcerda/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcerda/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcerda/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcerda/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcerda/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_BEGIN -->\n## Problem\n\nThe shared attribution workflow treated `` / `` as credit chrome and deleted them from the pull request description. The next description update could not find its section, so it appended a full second copy instead of replacing. Wilkes-Liberty/agency#28 ended up with three copies on 2026-10-17.\n\nDEV-1009.\n\n## Fix\n\n`clean_cursor_pr_body` now strips only removable attribution credit:\n\n- credit trailers and \"Generated with\" / robot-emoji lines\n- the trailing `cursor.com/agents` footer\n- Bugbot `CURSOR_SUMMARY` blocks\n\nThe `CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_*` HTML comments stay. A markers-only body is a no-op (no PATCH), so later updates remain idempotent.\n\nThe body scanner blanks those exact marker comments before matching, so the comments cannot trip the check. Real credit in commits, identities, the title, or the rest of the body still fails.\n\n## Test\n\n`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v` — 80 tests, all passing.\n\nRegression (strip + check):\n\n- Body with the section markers plus a credit trailer: markers kept, trailer removed, check passes.\n- Body with mid-prose authorship credit outside the markers: strip is a no-op, check still fails.\n\nExisting footer / `CURSOR_SUMMARY` cleanup still runs. Markers-only bodies are not rewritten.\n\n## Tag-bump rollout\n\nCallers pin `Wilkes-Liberty/shared-ci/.github/workflows/attribution.yml@v1`. Merging this PR does not change what they run. After merge, cut a patch release (v1.4.1 is the next unused patch on 1.4) and move the floating major tag. Do not retag from this PR.\n\n```sh\ngit tag -a v1.4.1 -m \"v1.4.1\"\ngit push origin v1.4.1\ngit tag -f v1 v1.4.1^{commit}\ngit push --force origin refs/tags/v1\ngit cat-file -t v1   # MUST print \"commit\"\n```\n\nThe `^{commit}` peel is load-bearing: pointing `v1` at the annotated tag object (instead of the commit) stops the org required-workflow rule from auto-triggering. One atomic force push, never delete-then-push.\n\nA changelog fragment is in `changelog.d/DEV-1009-keep-cursor-pr-body-markers.md` for the release-finalize compile.\n<!-- CURSOR_AGENT_PR_BODY_END -->\n\n<div><a href=\"https://cursor.com/agents/bc-7c91c14b-960c-5238-b219-d37074d6d895?cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_web\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-light.png\"><img alt=\"Open in Web\" width=\"114\" height=\"28\" src=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-web-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://cursor.com/background-agent?bcId=bc-7c91c14b-960c-5238-b219-d37074d6d895&cursor_ref=pr_footer&cursor_cta=open_in_cursor\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-light.png\"><img alt=\"Open in Cursor\" width=\"131\" height=\"28\" src=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/open-in-cursor-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> Scoped change to shared CI attribution scripts and workflow messaging; behavior is covered by new regression tests and does not touch auth or production runtime.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit b2c6f71dfb3b57cd70690b6032247be0d2fd020a. Bugbot is set up for automated code reviews on this repo. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-17T07:03:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T19:07:19Z","closed_at":"2026-10-17T21:14:41Z","merged_at":"2026-10-17T21:14:41Z","merge_commit_sha":"8d0f873feb9e0565347828e13f53589c2945c197","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"W